              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Email Content"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_EMAIL_CONTENT",
          "id": "1781611649706",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781611649707_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Fill only the communication parameters listed in {{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}.\n\nUse these parameter values:\nPlantName = {{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\nAge = {{$context.$variables.age}}\nUserName = {{$context.$user.$name}}\n\nUse this source data for execution quantity deviations:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_EMAIL_DATA.$output}}\n\nParameter mapping rules:\n\n1. ExecutionQuantityDeviationData\n- Read the source data from {{$context.$nodes.GET_EMAIL_DATA.$output}}.\n- Skip any deviation record that is null, empty, undefined, or does not contain usable deviation data.\n- For each valid deviation record, extract only:\n  - DeviationCategory\n  - PercentDeviation\n  - QuickMetrics\n  - YieldImpact\n- Map each valid record to this shape:\n  {\n    \"Category\": DeviationCategory,\n    \"Deviation\": PercentDeviation with exactly one % suffix,\n    \"Quick Metrics\": QuickMetrics,\n    \"Yield Impact\": YieldImpact\n  }\n- For Deviation, append % to PercentDeviation when PercentDeviation is present and does not already contain %.\n- If PercentDeviation already contains %, preserve it as-is and do not append another %.\n- If PercentDeviation is null, empty, blank, or undefined, leave Deviation empty.\n\n2. ExecutionQuantityDeviationSummaryData\nGenerate one operational description under 60 words from the same source data.\n\n- If there are no valid source records, or all valid records have PercentDeviation equal to 0, null, blank, or undefined and YieldImpact equal to No Variance, set ExecutionQuantityDeviationSummaryData to:\n\"No execution quantity deviations require supervisor or manufacturing engineering attention at this time.\"\n\n- If any valid record has a non-zero PercentDeviation or YieldImpact other than No Variance:\n  - Highlight the execution quantity deviations requiring attention.\n  - Mention affected ingredient, product, or resource categories where available.\n  - Include batch counts, PercentDeviation, QuickMetrics, and YieldImpact only when present in the source records.\n  - Provide practical next steps to validate execution records, review category details, and address variance drivers.\n  - Use a production supervisor or manufacturing engineer tone.\n  - Do not use phrases like \"the table\", \"below table\", \"displayed data\", \"below data\", or \"shown above\".\n\nGlobal rules:\n1. Fill only parameters present in {{$context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill}}.\n2. Preserve Age as a number.\n3. In ExecutionQuantityDeviationData, output Deviation with exactly one % suffix when PercentDeviation is present. Do not duplicate %.\n4. Do not include null, empty, or undefined deviation records in ExecutionQuantityDeviationData.\n5. Return only the FillParameters output.\n6. Do not include markdown, explanations, comments, or extra text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_MANUFACTUR_BATCHEXECUTIONQUANTITYDEVIATIONS",
